      <div type="clause" n="26.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 26.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="164" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ his scrift hit gecyþe þam biscope binnon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.3"/> XXX nihta, hweþer he to þære bote cirran wolde. Gif he swa ne dó, bete be þam þe se biscop him forgifan wille.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.star2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26.1" corresp="#wit-ld"><pb n="164" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ his scrift hit gecyþe ðær<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.1"/> bisceop<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.1"/> binnan þrittigum nihta, hwæþer he to þær<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.1"/> bote wille. Gif he swa ne do, bete swa se bisceop hine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.1"/> forgyfan wille.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="26.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="165" ed="#liebermann"/>Et presbiter hoc referat episcopo infra XXX noctes, utrum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.37"/> ad<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="38" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.38"/> emendationem et satisfactionem uelit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="39" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.39"/> (uenerit). Si non faciat hoc, emendet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="40" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.40"/> (componat) sicut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="41" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.41"/> episcopus ei condonare<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="42" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.42"/> uelit (concedet).<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.43"/></ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="26.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="142" ed="#attenborough"/>⁊ his scrift hit gecyþe þam biscope<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_26-1.attnote.fn.3"/> binnon XXX nihta, hweþer he to þære bote cirran wolde<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_26-1.attnote.fn.4"/>. Gif he swa ne dó, bete be þam þe se biscop<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_26-1.attnote.fn.5"/> him<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_26-1.attnote.fn.6"/> forgifan wille.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="165" ed="#liebermann"/>Und [dieser] sein Beichtvater melde es dem Bischofe binnen 30 Tagen, ob jener [Meineidige] sich hatte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.de.1"/> zur Busse bekehren wollen. Wenn er nicht so thut, büsse er, je nachdem ihm der Bischof gestatten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_26-1.lnote.de.2"/> will.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let his confessor report it to the bishop within 30 days, whether that [perjurer] had been willing to turn to penance. If he does not do so, let him pay compensation according to what the bishop will allow him.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="143" ed="#attenborough"/>And his confessor shall make known to the bishop within thirty days whether he has been willing to make amends. If he [the confessor] does not do so, he shall pay such compensation as the bishop is willing to allow him [to pay].</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="423" ed="#whitelock"/>And his confessor is to inform the bishop within 30 days whether he was willing to submit to that penance. If he does not do so, he is to pay in accordance with what the bishop will allow him.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">In H, V As follows in the same hand.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">164</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze Epilog aus Ld Quadr. Es folgt in derselben Hand</hi> V As.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply the Epilogue from Ld Quadr. There follows, in the same hand, V As.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.37" n="37" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">utrumque admend. <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">utrumque admend. Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.38" n="38" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.39" n="39" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">uelit <hi rend="italic">Lond RT;</hi> uenerit <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">uelit Lond RT; uenerit MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.40" n="40" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e. <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> co. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e. Lond; co. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.41" n="41" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">si <hi rend="italic">K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">si K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.42" n="42" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cond. u. <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> conc. [concedit <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi>] <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cond. u. Lond; conc. [concedit MHkBr] the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.oe.43" n="43" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">165</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Explicit hoc <hi rend="italic">fügt zu Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Lond adds Explicit hoc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Ld, Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> und Schmid verstehen: ‘ob Meineidiger büssen wolle (= werde). Wenn derselbe nicht’ usw.; danach also lebt der Meineidige noch, trotzt der vom Pfarrer auferlegten Pönitenz und empfängt nun strengere vom Bischof. Dagegen ist mit H Q <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi> vereinbar, als den Säumigen den Pfarrer zu betrachten, der die Pflicht hat, einem Reuigen christlich Grab zu schaffen. Letzterer Ansicht folge ich. Denn gerade diese Frist (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 12 d. e) von 30 Tagen tritt auch ein für die Überführung in ehrlich Grab, wenn man einen zu Unrecht verscharrten Verwandten reinigen will</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Ld, Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> and Schmid understand: ‘whether the perjurer wished (= would) do penance. If he does not’ etc.; on this view the perjurer is still alive, defies the penance imposed by the parish priest, and now receives a stricter one from the bishop. On the other hand, it is compatible with H and Q <hi rend="smallcaps">ii</hi> to regard the defaulter as the parish priest, whose duty it is to provide a Christian grave for a penitent. I follow the latter view. For precisely this period (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 12 d. e) of 30 days also applies to the transfer to an honourable grave when one wishes to clear a kinsman who has been wrongly buried without rites</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">107</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">nicht ‘vorschreiben’; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Geistliche 27 e</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">not ‘prescribe’; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Geistliche 27 e</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.attnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">142</biblScope></bibl><label>biscope</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þær bisceop</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">142</biblScope></bibl><label>wolde</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">bote wille</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">142</biblScope></bibl><label>biscop</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">bete swa se bisceop</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_26-1.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">142</biblScope></bibl><label>him</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hine</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
